+milestone: "2026.08.568"
+milestone_title: "Audited Promotion and Adaptive Continuous Learning"
+milestone_doc: openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md
+tasks:
+  - id: exp6561-v568-evidence-gate-contract
+    milestone: "2026.08.568"
+    deliverable: results/experiment_6561_v568_evidence_gate_contract.json
+    title: "V568 evidence eligibility, exclusion, model, and gate contract"
+    priority: critical
+    track: infrastructure-governance
+    requires_gpu: false
+    per_unit_rows: true
+    max_turns: 100
+    estimated_wall_time_min: 90
+    model: opus
+    prompt: |
+      CONTEXT
+      V567 completed Exp6548 through Exp6560. It produced reusable production, memory, saturation, and ARC assets. It also produced blocked CSL, saturation-audit, and GateMate records. V568 needs one additive evidence contract before it extends any lane. Work at {project_root}. The planning date is {date}.
+
+      EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST
+      - {project_root}/CODEX.md, {project_root}/CLAUDE.md, {project_root}/research-program.md, and {project_root}/openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md
+      - {project_root}/results/experiment_6548_v567_evidence_eligibility_contract.json through {project_root}/results/experiment_6560_v567_independent_capstone.json
+      - {project_root}/research-complete.yaml, {project_root}/research-references.md, {project_root}/ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml, and {project_root}/ops/conductor-log.md
+      - {project_root}/scripts/adversarial_verify.py, {project_root}/scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py, {project_root}/scripts/conductor_gates.py, and {project_root}/scripts/roadmap_schema.py
+      - {project_root}/_bmad/prd.md, {project_root}/_bmad/architecture.md, relevant capability specs, {project_root}/_bmad/traceability.md, and {project_root}/ops/e2e-test-plan.md
+
+      TASK
+      Build the additive V568 evidence and gate contract. Import V567 artifacts only by immutable path and hash. Freeze every V568 gate field, prior-failure entry, model requirement, and hardware boundary.
+
+      CONCRETE STEPS
+      0. PRECONDITIONS: record git status, CPU, RAM, disk, Python, Rust, PyO3, Z3, artifact paths and hashes, protected-file hashes, architecture freshness, and network status. This task performs no LLM load and no hardware command.
+      1. Add or confirm REQ-* and SCENARIO anchors for immutable evidence import, closed verdict classes, exact gate spelling, prior-failure completeness, model policy, hardware boundaries, and atomic terminal output. Write focused tests first.
+      2. Run live adversarial verification and row-consistency checks on Exp6548 through Exp6560. Record one eligibility row per artifact, including verifier version, exit status, stamped flags, live flags, and reason.
+      3. Mark Exp6557 as a conductor pre-gate block, not as a scientific audit. Mark Exp6553 and Exp6554 as blocked infrastructure evidence, not null science. Preserve the Exp6559 zero-command receipt.
+      4. Freeze all V568 task IDs, deliverables, readiness fields, gates, required artifact fields, sample floors, MODEL_SPECS, sequential-load rule, ARC no-solve rule, and zero-command hardware rule.
+      5. Confirm that each gate names a task in this roadmap and an identically spelled required field. Confirm that every scope-matched failed or retired task has all four prior-failure fields and that no `requires` chain uses a retired ID.
+      6. Attack missing artifacts, hash aliases, aggregate-only claims, stamped-versus-live verifier disagreement, missing gate fields, legacy-model substitution, impossible VRAM thresholds, retired-scope reuse, and protected-file mutation.
+      7. Set v568_evidence_contract_ready_score=1.0 only when the artifact, gate, prior-failure, model, hardware, and protected-file contracts all close. Set production_v567_evidence_ready_score=1.0 only when Exp6549 through Exp6551 remain eligible for a workload canary.
+      8. Write one terminal artifact atomically. Run focused tests, lint, spec coverage, exclusion-manifest lint, roadmap schema validation, row lint, adversarial verification, applicable E2E checks, and git status.
+
+      Required deliverable: {project_root}/results/experiment_6561_v568_evidence_gate_contract.json.
+      REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:
+        status:
+          principle: "A terminal state prevents a bootstrap record from posing as a completed evidence contract."
+        honest_verdict:
+          principle: "The verdict must state the eligible evidence boundary and use a terminal prefix."
+        verdict_class:
+          principle: "A closed class carries blocked, partial, null, and disqualified status into downstream aggregation."
+        v567_artifact_eligibility_rows:
+          principle: "One row per V567 artifact makes every import decision recheckable."
+        v568_gate_contract_rows:
+          principle: "Every downstream gate needs an in-roadmap task and an identically spelled upstream field."
+        prior_failure_contract_rows:
+          principle: "Each scope-matched failure needs experiment ID, verdict, changed method, and retirement signal."
+        model_and_sequential_runtime_contract:
+          principle: "The three mandated GGUF identities and actual-load rule must be frozen before outcomes exist."
+        hardware_claim_boundary:
+          principle: "The contract prevents unchanged GateMate commands and unauthenticated TSU claims."
+        v568_evidence_contract_ready_score:
+          principle: "One binary field gates tasks that need the complete V568 contract."
+        production_v567_evidence_ready_score:
+          principle: "The production canary needs a separate clean Exp6549-Exp6551 evidence gate."
+        per_unit_rows:
+          principle: "Artifact-level rows prevent one failed input from hiding inside an aggregate."
+        aggregate_row_recomputation:
+          principle: "Readiness fields must derive from emitted eligibility and contract rows."
+        gate_check_summary:
+          principle: "A blocked verdict must name the failed check and observed value."
+        preconditions_checked:
+          principle: "Resource and input receipts distinguish missing prerequisites from evidence failure."
+        protected_files_unchanged:
+          principle: "The task must not mutate research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py."
+        inference_substrate:
+          principle: "The artifact must declare immutable evidence aggregation with no new LLM inference."
+        verifier_is_oracle:
+          principle: "Artifact validation is audit authority and not oracle-distinct science."
+        field_provenance:
+          principle: "Every headline field must identify source rows, hashes, and reducers."
+        duration_s:
+          principle: "Monotonic wall time exposes skipped verifier and contract checks."
+        tests_run:
+          principle: "Named commands and exit codes make contract validation reproducible."
+        reproducibility_checksum:
+          principle: "A final content hash detects mutation of the terminal record."
+      Set inference_substrate=immutable_v567_artifact_gate_and_scope_audit_no_llm and verifier_is_oracle=true. A clean contract uses verdict_class=null, a usable subset uses partial, a missing input uses blocked, and false provenance uses disqualified.
+
+      Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python -m carnot.experiment_6561_v568_evidence_gate_contract --date {date}
+      Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
