+  - id: exp6562-constraint-saturation-independent-audit-v2
+    milestone: "2026.08.568"
+    deliverable: results/experiment_6562_constraint_saturation_independent_audit_v2.json
+    title: "Independent V567 constraint-saturation audit from checked-in rows"
+    priority: critical
+    track: infrastructure-audit
+    requires_gpu: false
+    per_unit_rows: true
+    max_turns: 50
+    estimated_wall_time_min: 120
+    agent_type: codex
+    model: gpt-5.5
+    prior_failures:
+      - experiment_id: exp6556-sota-constraint-saturation-intervention-ab
+        verdict: "complete_sota_constraint_saturation_intervention_positive: phase curve, bounded exact fallback benefit beyond longer flat, zero harmful intervention, charged cost, and receipts close"
+        addressed_by: "Exp6556 made the live comparative claim. This task performs no new generation and independently checks raw response provenance, model and GPU receipts, fixture proofs, exact clause and joint replay, pairing, harm, and charged cost from immutable rows."
+        retire_if_same_verdict: true
+      - experiment_id: exp6557-constraint-saturation-independent-audit
+        verdict: "blocked_gate_check_failed"
+        addressed_by: "Exp6557 never ran because the conductor rejected its missing prior-failure contract. This task includes complete prior-failure entries, has no structured gate, and audits the checked-in Exp6555 and Exp6556 evidence directly."
+        retire_if_same_verdict: true
+    prompt: |
+      CONTEXT
+      Exp6556 reports a positive constraint-saturation intervention. Exp6557 did not audit it because the conductor blocked the task before execution. The V567 capstone names this independent replay as the safe next experiment. This task must run before any new model inference. Work at {project_root}. The planning date is {date}.
+
+      EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST
+      - {project_root}/CODEX.md, {project_root}/CLAUDE.md, and the V568 roadmap document
+      - {project_root}/results/experiment_6555_proof_preserving_constraint_saturation_fixture.json and {project_root}/results/fixtures/v567_constraint_saturation.jsonl
+      - {project_root}/results/experiment_6556_sota_constraint_saturation_intervention_ab.json and {project_root}/results/checkpoints/experiment_6556_sota_constraint_saturation_intervention_ab.json
+      - {project_root}/python/carnot/experiment_6555_proof_preserving_constraint_saturation_fixture.py and {project_root}/python/carnot/experiment_6556_sota_constraint_saturation_intervention_ab.py
+      - exact fixture, clause, joint, response, model, GPU, token, cost, and reducer code plus their tests
+      - {project_root}/scripts/adversarial_verify.py, {project_root}/scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py, relevant specs, exclusions, traceability, and E2E plan
+
+      TASK
+      Independently audit the V567 saturation claim from checked-in evidence. Perform no new LLM generation. Rule separately on fixture validity, live model provenance, exact results, phase curves, paired interventions, harm, and cost.
+
+      CONCRETE STEPS
+      0. PRECONDITIONS: record input existence, paths and hashes, raw-response and checkpoint paths, model-file hashes without loading weights, checker hashes, Python and Z3 versions, CPU, RAM, disk, audit seed, and protected-file hashes.
+      1. Add or confirm REQ-* and SCENARIO anchors for independent fixture proof, live-receipt validation, clause replay, joint replay, paired recomputation, harm, charged cost, missing inputs, and atomic output. Write tests first.
+      2. Replay every equivalent and hardened fixture row against the source exact solver. Confirm constraint count, clause identity, interaction, surface, lineage, and intended proof relation.
+      3. Validate each model file hash, process command, PID, start and end time, GPU sample, token count, response hash, exit status, and raw response. A loader smoke flag or self-reported process ID is not enough. Reject synthetic response text, constant fake GPU samples, stale outputs, and impossible timing.
+      4. Replay every clause and joint result. Confirm that every decomposition preserves every clause and that every released result passed the exact joint checker.
+      5. Recompute per-model and pooled phase curves, matched flat-versus-long-flat effects, decomposition and fallback effects, recoveries, regressions, harmful interventions, tokens, solver calls, retries, wall time, timeouts, and censoring from rows only.
+      6. Attack missing and duplicate rows, unequal cells, hidden retries, zero-headroom wins, aggregate tampering, post-held thresholds, model identity shortcuts, invalid releases, and circular exact authority.
+      7. Set constraint_saturation_independent_audit_ready_score=1.0 only when fixture, live provenance, row closure, exact replay, pairing, harm, cost, and verdict recomputation all pass. Set constraint_saturation_policy_audited_score=1.0 only when the independent audit confirms the bounded policy claim.
+      8. Write one terminal artifact atomically. Run focused tests, lint, spec coverage, row lint, adversarial verification, exact-replay E2E checks, and git status.
+
+      Required deliverable: {project_root}/results/experiment_6562_constraint_saturation_independent_audit_v2.json.
+      REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:
+        status:
+          principle: "An always-run audit needs a terminal state for clean, missing, invalid, and non-recomputable evidence."
+        honest_verdict:
+          principle: "The verdict must state fixture, live provenance, exact replay, harm, cost, and policy dispositions with a terminal prefix."
+        verdict_class:
+          principle: "A closed class prevents an audit record from becoming unbounded positive science."
+        input_existence_and_hash_receipts:
+          principle: "The audit must identify the exact artifacts, checkpoints, raw responses, and checkers it used."
+        independent_fixture_proof_rows:
+          principle: "The model comparison is ineligible if the proof-preserving variants do not replay."
+        independent_live_provenance_rows:
+          principle: "Commands, PIDs, GPU samples, tokens, and response hashes must prove actual flagship inference."
+        independent_clause_and_joint_replay_rows:
+          principle: "Every credited success and release needs a separate executable replay."
+        independent_phase_curve_rows:
+          principle: "Constraint-load collapse must be recomputed by model, count, type, interaction, and surface."
+        independent_paired_intervention_rows:
+          principle: "Every claimed benefit needs matched rows against flat and longer-flat controls."
+        harmful_intervention_and_release_audit:
+          principle: "No aggregate gain can hide regressions or one invalid release."
+        charged_cost_audit:
+          principle: "Tokens, retries, solver calls, and time must recompute from raw receipts."
+        constraint_saturation_independent_audit_ready_score:
+          principle: "One binary field states whether the V567 saturation evidence is independently usable."
+        constraint_saturation_policy_audited_score:
+          principle: "A separate field distinguishes clean null evidence from a confirmed promotable policy."
+        per_unit_rows:
+          principle: "Every audit conclusion needs unit-level recomputation rows."
+        aggregate_row_recomputation:
+          principle: "The audit verdict must derive only from independent rows."
+        gate_check_summary:
+          principle: "A blocked audit must name every missing or failed check and observed value."
+        preconditions_checked:
+          principle: "Input and replay receipts distinguish blocked audit work from null science."
+        protected_files_unchanged:
+          principle: "The audit must not repair upstream evidence or mutate protected orchestration files."
+        inference_substrate:
+          principle: "The audit replays stored evidence and performs no new GGUF generation."
+        verifier_is_oracle:
+          principle: "Independent executable replay is audit authority, so a clean audit uses a non-positive class."
+        field_provenance:
+          principle: "Each disposition must point to immutable rows, receipts, and reducers."
+        random_seed:
+          principle: "A fixed audit order makes attacks and samples repeatable."
+        duration_s:
+          principle: "Monotonic time exposes an audit that skipped receipt or replay work."
+        tests_run:
+          principle: "Named tests and E2E commands show independent checks executed."
+        reproducibility_checksum:
+          principle: "A final hash protects the independent determination trail."
+      Set inference_substrate=independent_checked_in_sota_receipt_and_exact_constraint_replay_no_new_llm and verifier_is_oracle=true. Use verdict_class=null for a clean audit, partial for incomplete but usable evidence, blocked for missing inputs, or disqualified for false provenance, invalid variants, missing clauses, or non-recomputable claims.
+
+      Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python -m carnot.experiment_6562_constraint_saturation_independent_audit_v2 --date {date}
+      Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
