+      - current pipeline regression fixtures, workload manifests, exact verifier code, relevant tests, specs, traceability, exclusions, status, changelog, and E2E plan
+
+      TASK
+      Run a native, disabled-adapter, enabled-adapter, forced-abstain, forced-fallback, and rollback canary on production-shaped verification workloads. Measure actual work and exact outputs.
+
+      CONCRETE STEPS
+      0. PRECONDITIONS: evaluate the structured gate and record expected and observed values, upstream path and hash, fixture hashes, Python and Z3 versions, CPU, RAM, disk, process isolation, timer resolution, and protected-file hashes.
+      1. Add or confirm REQ-* and SCENARIO anchors for real-workload identity, measured cost, candidate preservation, abstention, fallback, persistence, restart, rollback, and atomic output. Write tests first.
+      2. Freeze a family-blind production workload matrix before execution. Include normal, empty, malformed, unsupported, fallback-heavy, exception, restart, and rollback strata. Use current checked-in fixtures only.
+      3. Compare native, disabled, enabled, forced-abstain, forced-fallback, and rollback conditions with identical requests, candidate order, warm-up, seeds, process placement, and exact checks.
+      4. Record request bytes, route, abstention, candidate set and order, exact result, checker calls, serialization bytes, persistence bytes, process time, monotonic wall time, fallback reason, and rollback state for every unit.
+      5. Exclude synthetic adapter cost units from the headline. Report them only as a diagnostic. Use direct receipts for work and latency claims.
+      6. Attack outcome leakage, model or family identity, source IDs, entity names, row order, exception writes, candidate deletion, hidden retries, unreachable fallback, timer bias, cache imbalance, and rollback drift.
+      7. Set production_workload_canary_ready_score=1.0 only when disabled identity, exact equality, candidate preservation, fallback, restart, and rollback all pass with complete rows. Set production_workload_promotion_candidate_score=1.0 only when enabled routing improves preregistered measured work or latency without a safety, tail-latency, or invalid-release regression.
